sequenceDiagram
    participant Product as Product<br>[implements GapCentralResponse]
    participant CN as CN Central<br>[implements GapCentral]

    Note over Product, CN: Precondition: connected,<br>IoCapabilities set for passkey entry<br>(display and/or keyboard).

    Product->>CN: GapCentral.PairAndBond()

    alt CN displays passkey, user enters it on peer
        CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.AuthenticationRequired(<br>isNumericComparison=false, passkey=485923)
        Note over Product: Display 485923. User reads it and types it on the peer device.<br>No AuthenticateWithPasskey call is required on our side.

        alt Peer accepts the correct passkey
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.NumberOfBondsChanged(1)
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=true)
        else Peer enters wrong passkey
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(<br>pairedSuccessfully=false, reason=passkeyEntryFailed)
        end
    else Peer displays passkey, user enters it on us
        CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.AuthenticationRequired(<br>isNumericComparison=false)
        Note over Product: passkey field is unused in this variant.<br>User reads the passkey shown on the peer and types it into the Product UI.

        Product->>CN: GapCentral.AuthenticateWithPasskey(485923)

        alt Correct passkey
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.NumberOfBondsChanged(1)
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=true)
        else Wrong passkey
            CN-->>Product: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(<br>pairedSuccessfully=false, reason=passkeyEntryFailed)
        end
    end

    Note over Product, CN: In both variants, no response within the 30 s SMP timeout results in<br>PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=false, reason=timeout).
